message.content:
Sure! Below is a simple example of an “interactive card” that rotates when you hover over it.  
It uses only **HTML** and **CSS** (no JavaScript).  

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* Basic reset */
* { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

/* Container that centers the card */
body {
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    height:100vh;
    background:#f0f0f0;
}

/* The card itself */
.card {
    width:250px;
    height:350px;
    perspective:800px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D transform */
    cursor:pointer;
}

/* Front & back faces */
.card__inner {
    position:relative;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    transition:transform .6s ease-in-out;
    transform-style:preserve-3d;
}

.card:hover .card__inner {
    transform:rotateY(180deg);   /* Rotate 180° around Y‑axis on hover */
}

/* Common face styles */
.card__face {
    position:absolute;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;   /* Hide the backside when rotated */
    border-radius:12px;
    overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

/* Front face */
.card__front {
    background:#fff;
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

/* Back face */
.card__back {
    background:#fafafa;
    transform:rotateY(180deg);   /* Start rotated so it’s hidden initially */
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

/* Example content */
.card__image {
    width:80%;
    height:auto;
    border-radius:8px;
    margin-bottom:15px;
}
.card__title {
    font-size:1.5rem;
    color:#333;
    margin-bottom:10px;
}
.card__text {
    font-size:1rem;
    color:#666;
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card">
    <div class="card__inner">
        <!-- Front side -->
        <div class="card__face card__front">
            <img src="https://picsum.photos/200/150" alt="Sample Image" class="card__image">
            <h3 class="card__title">Front Title</h3>
            <p class="card__text">This is the front side of the card.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Back side -->
        <div class="card__face card__back">
            <h3 class="card__title">Back Title</h3>
            <p class="card__text">Here is some more information on the back.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

1. **Perspective** – The `.card` container has `perspective:800px;`.  
   This gives the 3D rotation a realistic depth effect.

2. **Transform style** – The inner wrapper `.card__inner` uses  
   `transform-style: preserve-3d;` so its children keep their 3D positions.

3. **Rotation** – On hover, we apply `transform: rotateY(180deg);` to the inner wrapper.  
   The back face is pre‑rotated with `transform: rotateY(180deg);` so it becomes visible after the flip.

4. **Backface visibility** – Setting `backface-visibility:hidden;` hides each face when it’s turned away from the viewer.

Feel free to replace the placeholder image, titles, or text with your own content. Enjoy the rotating card!
